      "fullsize": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_fullsize/plain/did:plc:hu35oubkccqrxl4ldgczpgw7/bafkreib2gc45ajyprexvehouisq4nlqh4fhegsknd2da2xkadykghsjiuq",
      "alt": "Taken together, what these three books demonstrate is that robots, AI, and other seemingly social and intelligent artifacts are not just one more technological challenge to which we need to apply existing moral and legal thinking. They are and they do much more than that. They provide the opportunity for and provoke the need to reassess and reevaluate all aspects of what comprises and justifies these moral and legal affordances, questioning what is often taken for granted and thereby goes by without notice.\nThis is the unique impact and significance of the machine question. It is a question not just of ethics applied to the exceptional opportunities and challenges of emerging technology. It is a question that concerns the very foundation and integrity of ethics itself.",
